1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,495
Listing day gets the headlines.

2
00:00:02,495 --> 00:00:04,590
But the real commitment starts

3
00:00:04,590 --> 00:00:05,580
the day after.

4
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:07,442
Here's what life looks like

5
00:00:07,442 --> 00:00:09,071
as a listed company in

6
00:00:09,071 --> 00:00:11,225
Zimbabwe. This is Reian Creative

7
00:00:11,225 --> 00:00:13,145
Finance. Understanding markets.

8
00:00:13,145 --> 00:00:14,309
Following capital.

9
00:00:14,659 --> 00:00:16,357
First, you have new owners.

10
00:00:16,357 --> 00:00:18,604
Ordinary shares usually carry votes

11
00:00:18,604 --> 00:00:19,864
at general meetings,

12
00:00:19,864 --> 00:00:22,275
where shareholders elect directors and

13
00:00:22,275 --> 00:00:23,754
approve major decisions.

14
00:00:23,754 --> 00:00:25,617
Dividends are paid only when

15
00:00:25,617 --> 00:00:27,425
the board declares them out

16
00:00:27,425 --> 00:00:29,507
of profits. Nothing is guaranteed.

17
00:00:29,857 --> 00:00:31,533
Then the reporting calendar.

18
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:32,843
On both the ZSE and

19
00:00:32,843 --> 00:00:34,624
the VFEX, interim results are

20
00:00:34,624 --> 00:00:36,300
due within three months of

21
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:37,452
the half year end.

22
00:00:37,452 --> 00:00:39,338
Audited annual results must be

23
00:00:39,338 --> 00:00:41,329
published within three months of

24
00:00:41,329 --> 00:00:42,848
year end, and the annual

25
00:00:42,848 --> 00:00:44,943
report sent to shareholders within

26
00:00:44,943 --> 00:00:46,462
six months, and at least

27
00:00:46,462 --> 00:00:48,086
21 days before the annual

28
00:00:48,086 --> 00:00:50,234
general meeting. And price sensitive

29
00:00:50,234 --> 00:00:52,172
news must be disclosed promptly.

30
00:00:52,522 --> 00:00:54,228
Now your share price and

31
00:00:54,228 --> 00:00:56,559
market capitalisation. Market cap is

32
00:00:56,559 --> 00:00:58,491
simply shares in issue times

33
00:00:58,491 --> 00:00:59,572
the share price,

34
00:00:59,572 --> 00:01:01,505
and it changes every trading

35
00:01:01,505 --> 00:01:03,438
day. Our example company from

36
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:05,200
part three has 40 million

37
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,792
shares. At 50 cents it's

38
00:01:06,792 --> 00:01:08,441
worth 20 million dollars.

39
00:01:08,441 --> 00:01:09,293
At 60 cents,

40
00:01:09,293 --> 00:01:10,942
24 million. A weak share

41
00:01:10,942 --> 00:01:12,648
price can make it harder

42
00:01:12,648 --> 00:01:14,069
to raise money later.

43
00:01:14,419 --> 00:01:16,527
Governance matters even more after

44
00:01:16,527 --> 00:01:18,530
listing. Investors expect a board

45
00:01:18,530 --> 00:01:20,111
that challenges management,

46
00:01:20,111 --> 00:01:21,956
including independent directors,

47
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:23,959
audit and remuneration committees,

48
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:25,698
clear rules on conflicts of

49
00:01:25,698 --> 00:01:27,701
interest and related party deals,

50
00:01:27,701 --> 00:01:29,546
and an annual general meeting

51
00:01:29,546 --> 00:01:31,707
where shareholders can question the

52
00:01:31,707 --> 00:01:32,919
board face to face.

53
00:01:32,919 --> 00:01:34,869
Remember Nvidia from our global

54
00:01:34,869 --> 00:01:37,136
markets episode: when governance fails,

55
00:01:37,136 --> 00:01:38,717
the share price feels it.

56
00:01:39,067 --> 00:01:40,860
A listing also opens doors.

57
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:42,205
A company can do a

58
00:01:42,205 --> 00:01:44,335
rights issue, offering new shares

59
00:01:44,335 --> 00:01:46,296
to existing shareholders first.

60
00:01:46,296 --> 00:01:47,809
It can use its shares

61
00:01:47,809 --> 00:01:49,378
to pay for acquisitions,

62
00:01:49,378 --> 00:01:51,675
reward staff through employee share

63
00:01:51,675 --> 00:01:53,749
schemes, and it gains visibility

64
00:01:53,749 --> 00:01:55,430
with lenders and partners.

65
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:57,162
So it's a trade off.

66
00:01:57,162 --> 00:01:58,025
On one side:

67
00:01:58,025 --> 00:01:59,234
access to capital,

68
00:01:59,234 --> 00:02:00,616
liquidity for owners,

69
00:02:00,616 --> 00:02:02,689
credibility and shares you can

70
00:02:02,689 --> 00:02:03,955
use as a currency.

71
00:02:03,955 --> 00:02:04,877
On the other:

72
00:02:04,877 --> 00:02:06,489
ongoing compliance costs,

73
00:02:06,489 --> 00:02:08,619
public scrutiny of every result,

74
00:02:08,619 --> 00:02:10,058
some loss of control,

75
00:02:10,058 --> 00:02:12,016
and pressure from the market

76
00:02:12,016 --> 00:02:13,167
every single day.

77
00:02:13,517 --> 00:02:15,485
And you're always being watched.

78
00:02:15,485 --> 00:02:17,508
The exchange enforces its rules,

79
00:02:17,508 --> 00:02:19,913
the Securities and Exchange Commission

80
00:02:19,913 --> 00:02:21,170
oversees the market,

81
00:02:21,170 --> 00:02:23,083
and the Reserve Bank's foreign

82
00:02:23,083 --> 00:02:25,707
exchange rules cover foreign shareholdings

83
00:02:25,707 --> 00:02:27,183
and any listing abroad,

84
00:02:27,183 --> 00:02:29,151
which needs its prior approval.

85
00:02:29,151 --> 00:02:31,010
Serious breaches can lead to

86
00:02:31,010 --> 00:02:32,759
your shares being suspended.

87
00:02:33,109 --> 00:02:34,743
Finally, the exit doors.

88
00:02:34,743 --> 00:02:36,620
A suspension halts trading,

89
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:38,798
often because results are late

90
00:02:38,798 --> 00:02:40,614
or information is unclear.

91
00:02:40,614 --> 00:02:43,035
Delisting means the company leaves

92
00:02:43,035 --> 00:02:45,214
the exchange, either voluntarily,

93
00:02:45,214 --> 00:02:46,909
for example to move to

94
00:02:46,909 --> 00:02:49,088
another exchange, or because it

95
00:02:49,088 --> 00:02:50,964
no longer meets the rules.

96
00:02:50,964 --> 00:02:52,114
TSL, for example,

97
00:02:52,114 --> 00:02:53,870
was reported to end its

98
00:02:53,870 --> 00:02:55,685
ZSE listing in June 2026

99
00:02:55,685 --> 00:02:57,259
and move to the VFEX.

100
00:02:57,609 --> 00:02:59,074
Listing is a marriage,

101
00:02:59,074 --> 00:03:00,031
not a wedding.

102
00:03:00,031 --> 00:03:01,214
Prepare for years,

103
00:03:01,214 --> 00:03:02,960
report on time every time,

104
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,988
and treat your shareholders as

105
00:03:04,988 --> 00:03:06,735
partners. That's the end of

106
00:03:06,735 --> 00:03:08,256
our road to the stock

107
00:03:08,256 --> 00:03:10,565
exchange series. This is educational

108
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:12,649
content, not legal or investment

109
00:03:12,649 --> 00:03:15,015
advice. Follow Reian Creative Finance

110
00:03:15,015 --> 00:03:15,635
for more.
